   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c64b8aa1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Simulation and replay\n",
    "Simulation is at the heart of the library. It relies on a model of the laws of physics which will allow you to simulate a bicycle journey based on the parameters you have specified.\n",
    "\n",
    "In future mode : \n",
    "\n",
    "A given route is composed of several short segments. Within each segment, your assumed power output will be determined based on:\n",
    "\n",
    "- wind conditions (wind speed and angle relative to the direction of travel),\n",
    "\n",
    "- terrain conditions (gradient, turns),\n",
    "\n",
    "- your adaptation to the context as defined in the behavior settings.\n",
    "\n",
    "Your final speed will be calculated according to the laws of physics, based on this power output and your initial speed at the start of the segment.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "To start a simulation you must "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b5626d8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Input data \n",
    " To simulate a bicycle journey based on the parameters you have specified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "ecb7877d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from refwindcycle.core import Simulator\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c332264",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Creating a simulator object will require entering a set of parameters, some of which are customized to the cyclist and the bicycle.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Simulator parameters\n",
    "### Behavior Profiles \n",
    "The behavioral profile allows for power adjustments during simulations, adapting the cyclist's power output to uphills, downhills, and corners. \n",
    "\n",
    "Wind is itself considered a virtual elevation gain (positive or negative) and is implicitly integrated into the behavioral parameters associated with uphills and downhills.\n",
    "\n",
    "Three behavioral types are defined: 'realistic', 'conservative', and 'aggressive'.The behavioral type defines the power variations according to the gradient or the angle of the turn.\n",
    "\n",
    "Different behavioral types can be applied to uphills, downhills, and corners.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a quick start, there are 3 predefined profiles: \n",
    "\n",
    "| Profile name  | Uphill behavior | Downhill behavior | Corner behavior |\n",
    "| ---- | --- | --- | --- | \n",
    "| **amateur** | conservative |conservative| conservative|\n",
    "| **competitive**| realistic|realistic|realistic|\n",
    "| **pro** | aggressive|aggressive|aggressive|\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following I will chose a competitive profile and display its content : "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "a0dfa7d0",
   "metadata": {},
