   "source": [
    "#\n",
    "# before calling the simulator weather must be initalized \n",
    "# see chapter weather of the documentation \n",
    "from datetime import timedelta, datetime\n",
    "from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\n",
    "from refwindcycle.weather import WeatherProvider\n",
    "from refwindcycle.weather.grib_finder import build_grib_list\n",
    "from refwindcycle.analysis import RouteAnalyzer\n",
    "\n",
    "origin_tz = ZoneInfo(\"Europe/Paris\")\n",
    "t_start=datetime.fromisoformat(\"2026-02-12 02:30:00\").replace(tzinfo=origin_tz)\n",
    "gribs_list = build_grib_list(\".'\", t_start, 3, 6)\n",
    "weather = WeatherProvider(gribs_list, bcache=True)\n",
    "mygrib = weather.grib\n",
    "# a gpx file must also be loaded and preprocessed\n",
    "# see chapter gpx of the documentation \n",
    "analyzer = RouteAnalyzer() \n",
    "gpx_result = analyzer.process_gpx(\"./E20250914-109K-0743.gpx\")\n",
    "segments = gpx_result.segments\n",
    "#            \n",
    "# parameters cda, crr and weight for the rider+bike system (just examples, you should use your own estimates)\n",
    "my_cda=0.500\n",
    "my_crr=0.004\n",
    "my_mass=80\n",
    "# ============================================================================================\n",
    "# Now I can create a simulator object with this profile and run it with the weather data I have\n",
    "# ============================================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "sim_wind = Simulator(\n",
    "    grib=mygrib, # this is the weather data I have, in grib format, that I will use for the simulation\n",
    "    behavior=my_profile,\n",
    "    CdA=my_cda,\n",
    "    Cr=my_crr,\n",
    "    m=my_mass\n",
    "   )\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90fcfb27",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "The object simulator is now available. We can then either replay a route on the date it was completed, or fictitiously project a route on any date.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Replaying the route\n",
    "\n",
    "We can replay our route by calling the `simulate_replay` method. This method will replay our route, respecting the observed speed and timing, and analyzing the wind throughout the entire route. \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "The simulation results will include all the elements related to time, speed, observed wind, and also an average power calculated based on the terrain's elevation and the wind's influence.\n",
    "\n",
    "To perform a replay:\n",
    "\n",
    "**You must have a GPX file including timestamps**. The timestamp values ​​in the GPX file indicate the time of passage at each point on the track.\n",
    "\n",
    "Tracking applications generally allow you to retrieve your GPX tracks with timestamps. However, timestamps are not usually available when you retrieve someone else's track. For example, if you download a GPX file from Pogacar or, even, from one of your friend on the Strava app, you won't have their travel times.\n"
   ]
  },
